From: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:10:00 +0800
Subject: touchpad: support INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD

Backport the upstream support for the INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD input
property, which is what upstream uses to mark a haptic touchpad (also
called pressure pad or forcepad) as such.

Three pieces are needed and they come from upstream:

  a) The vendored linux headers do not define
     INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD (0x07). Upstream added it in
     7621edab ("include: sync headers with kernel 6.18"), so do the
     same here or the new code below does not compile.

  b) parse_input_prop_property() resolves AttrInputProp entries by name
     through libevdev_property_from_name(). libevdev < 1.13.6 does not
     know "INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD" and returns -1, which makes the
     parser fail. Upstream added a name-specific fallback in db6a0466
     ("touchpad: use INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD as signal it's a
     pressurepad"); without it a quirk using this property makes
     libinput discard the *entire* quirks database, which is the bug
     behind the reverted debian patch (see PR #8).

  c) tp_init_pressurepad() only looked at the ABS_MT_PRESSURE resolution
     and at ModelPressurePad. Upstream made it honour
     INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD as well in db6a0466, so a device marked by
     the property actually gets the pressure axes disabled.

Keeping QUIRK_MODEL_PRESSURE_PAD is deliberate: the ModelPressurePad
quirk stays valid for this version, and the existing quirks that use it
(e.g. Lenovo ThinkBook G6+/G7+, HONOR MagicBook Art 14) must keep
working.

Forwarded: not-needed (backport of 7621edab + db6a0466)
Signed-off-by: lichenggang <lichenggang@uniontech.com>
---
 include/linux/freebsd/input-event-codes.h | 1 +
 include/linux/linux/input-event-codes.h   | 1 +
 src/evdev-mt-touchpad.c                   | 3 ++-
 src/util-prop-parsers.c                   | 10 ++++++++--
 4 files changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/include/linux/freebsd/input-event-codes.h b/include/linux/freebsd/input-event-codes.h
index 0c2e27d..37f8e48 100644
--- a/include/linux/freebsd/input-event-codes.h
+++ b/include/linux/freebsd/input-event-codes.h
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #define INPUT_PROP_TOPBUTTONPAD		0x04	/* softbuttons at top of pad */
 #define INPUT_PROP_POINTING_STICK	0x05	/* is a pointing stick */
 #define INPUT_PROP_ACCELEROMETER	0x06	/* has accelerometer */
+#define INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD		0x07	/* pressure triggers clicks */
 
 #define INPUT_PROP_MAX			0x1f
 #define INPUT_PROP_CNT			(INPUT_PROP_MAX + 1)
diff --git a/include/linux/linux/input-event-codes.h b/include/linux/linux/input-event-codes.h
index 0c2e27d..37f8e48 100644
--- a/include/linux/linux/input-event-codes.h
+++ b/include/linux/linux/input-event-codes.h
@@ -27,6 +27,7 @@
 #define INPUT_PROP_TOPBUTTONPAD		0x04	/* softbuttons at top of pad */
 #define INPUT_PROP_POINTING_STICK	0x05	/* is a pointing stick */
 #define INPUT_PROP_ACCELEROMETER	0x06	/* has accelerometer */
+#define INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD		0x07	/* pressure triggers clicks */
 
 #define INPUT_PROP_MAX			0x1f
 #define INPUT_PROP_CNT			(INPUT_PROP_MAX + 1)
diff --git a/src/evdev-mt-touchpad.c b/src/evdev-mt-touchpad.c
index 909e8f0..14dcbc4 100644
--- a/src/evdev-mt-touchpad.c
+++ b/src/evdev-mt-touchpad.c
@@ -3733,7 +3733,8 @@ tp_init_pressurepad(struct tp_dispatch *tp,
 	 *
 	 * See also #562
 	 */
-	if (libevdev_get_abs_resolution(device->evdev, ABS_MT_PRESSURE) != 0 ||
+	if (libevdev_has_property(device->evdev, INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD) ||
+	    libevdev_get_abs_resolution(device->evdev, ABS_MT_PRESSURE) != 0 ||
 	    evdev_device_has_model_quirk(device, QUIRK_MODEL_PRESSURE_PAD)) {
 		libevdev_disable_event_code(device->evdev, EV_ABS, ABS_MT_PRESSURE);
 		libevdev_disable_event_code(device->evdev, EV_ABS, ABS_PRESSURE);
diff --git a/src/util-prop-parsers.c b/src/util-prop-parsers.c
index fc829e9..084cf4a 100644
--- a/src/util-prop-parsers.c
+++ b/src/util-prop-parsers.c
@@ -465,8 +465,14 @@ parse_input_prop_property(const char *prop, struct input_prop *props_out, size_t
 				goto out;
 		} else {
 			int val = libevdev_property_from_name(s);
-			if (val == -1)
-				goto out;
+			if (val == -1) {
+				/* Remove once we require libevdev 1.13.6 */
+				if (streq(s, "INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD")) {
+					val = INPUT_PROP_PRESSUREPAD;
+				} else {
+					goto out;
+				}
+			}
 			prop = (unsigned int)val;
 		}
 		props[idx].prop = prop;
